 Sound good? We’re hiring! Join our team!

 Recruitment privacy policy

Automattic, the tech powerhouse behind [WordPress.com](https://wordpress.com/), [Jetpack](https://jetpack.com/), [Tumblr](http://www.tumblr.com), and [WooCommerce](https://woocommerce.com/), is looking for the world’s best systems engineers. On our Systems team, you’ll deliver high availability, performance, and security for tens of billions of page views and over a billion web surfers each month—from [30 private data centers](https://automattic.com/automattic-data-centers/) in 30 locations on 6 continents. Help us develop, build, and maintain a leading global infrastructure and share our learnings with the world.

As part of a small and vertically integrated team responsible for a huge setup, you’ll have a unique opportunity to participate in all aspects of the management of our infrastructure, including:

- Maximizing the availability and uptime of all services through proactive planning, sound architectural decisions, automation and rapid response to failures;
- Making Automattic services as fast as possible for our users through optimization of server-side and client-side interactions, and work with 3rd party services where necessary;
- Ensuring our services are safe and secure for both our users and employees through a combination of proactive monitoring and enforcement, real-time response, and maintaining data integrity/backups to allow recovery from disasters;
- Removing as much friction as possible between Automattic developers and their goal of shipping software. When there are questions, we provide answers—usually in a matter of minutes, sometimes seconds;

Here’s a real-time traffic map. Each color represents an Automattic data center: [https://automattic.com/automattic-data-centers](https://automattic.wordpress.com/?page_id=237636&preview=true)

**The Systems Engineer position might be a good fit if you:**

- Have maintained large Nginx setups with advanced routing configuration, load balancing, reliable performance and high availability;
- Have run very large MySQL/MariaDB deployments while maintaining an unparalleled level of performance, uptime and data integrity;
- Have experience running and debugging PHP applications at scale;
- Understand the relationship of these services with the lower level systems stacks – filesystems, network, memory management, kernel internals, etc;
- Have deep operational and maintenance experience with very large and complex public facing web hosting systems;
- Can autonomously architect, prototype, and maintain solutions to different problems and hosting requirements;
- Possess extreme attention to detail and strive for unparalleled operational excellence;
- Are open and available for a 2-3 week post-COVID travel per year to meet up with your teammates in person.

**Want to know more about how we do things? Watch:**

 We are looking to expand our team and aim to reflect and expand on the diversity of Automatticians currently working with us. At Automattic, we value diversity and know that different perspectives will ensure our team is innovative and creative thinking.

**Salary range: $120,000-$180,000+ USD.** Please note that salary ranges are global, regardless of location, and we pay in local currency.

We are searching for high-caliber candidates with the skills and qualities to have a net positive for Automattic. Pay will reflect the potential contribution and the impact you can bring, which may, in some cases, go beyond the range stated for the right candidate.

We’re pleased to offer a straightforward, competitive base salary, providing financial clarity without complex variable components. This isn’t your typical work-from-home job: we are a fully-remote company with an open vacation policy. To see a full list of benefits by country, consult our [Benefits Page](https://automattic.com/benefits/). And check out these links to learn more about [How We Hire](https://automattic.com/how-we-hire/) and [What We Expect from Ourselves](https://automattic.com/expectations/). #LI-DNI

#### About Automattic

Now in [our 20th year](https://timeline.automattic.com/), we’re the people behind [WordPress.com](http://wordpress.com/), [WooCommerce](https://href.li/?http://woocommerce.com/), [Beeper](https://www.beeper.com/), [Tumblr](https://href.li/?https://www.tumblr.com/), [Simplenote](https://href.li/?http://simplenote.com/), [Jetpack](https://href.li/?http://jetpack.com/), [Longreads](https://href.li/?http://longreads.com/), [Day One](https://href.li/?https://dayoneapp.com/), [PocketCasts](https://href.li/?https://www.pocketcasts.com/), and more. We believe in making the web a better place.

We’re a distributed company with more than 1500 Automatticians in nearly every corner of the globe, speaking over a hundred different languages. Enriched by this diversity, we’re united by a singular mission: to democratize publishing, commerce, and messaging so anyone with a story can tell it, anyone with a product can sell it, and everyone can manage their communications from a single source. In short, we help maintain a balance in society, creating and continually refining powerful tools people can use to compete fairly—regardless of income, gender, politics, language, or where they live in the world.

[We believe in Open Source](https://github.com/Automattic), and the vast majority of our work is available under the [GPL](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_General_Public_License). Automattic is a [Most Loved Company](https://mostlovedworkplace.com/companies/automattic-inc/), an Equal Opportunity employer, and [Disability Confident Committed](https://disabilityconfident.campaign.gov.uk/). ([Here’s what that might mean for you](https://happinessengineer.blog/2022/09/08/happiness-for-everyone-working-with-a-disability-at-automattic/).) If you need accommodations during the application or interview process, please [fill out this form](https://automattic.com/application-accommodation-request/). We are committed to ensuring an accessible hiring process for all candidates. Learn more about our [Employee Resource Groups](https://automattic.com/automattician-resource-groups/).

You can track your application status and more at [MyGreenhouse](https://my.greenhouse.io/users/sign_in).

To learn about how we handle your data, please review our [Job Applicant & Candidate Privacy Notice](https://automattic.com/automattic-job-applicant-candidate-privacy-notice/) and our [Privacy Policy](https://automattic.com/privacy/).

_All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. View the “Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal” poster_ [_here_](https://automattic.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/22-088_eeoc_knowyourrights6.12.pdf)_. Automattic participates in the_ [_E-Verify program_](https://automattic.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/e-verify_participation_poster_eng_es.pdf) _in certain locations, as required by law_.

Zimmer Biomet is one of the world’s leading Orthopaedics medical device companies. Our innovations help treat patients suffering from disorders of, or injuries to, bones, joints or supporting soft tissues. It is our mission to alleviate pain and improve the quality of life for people around the world: a patient’s mobility is enhanced by a Zimmer Biomet product or technology every 8 seconds. As part of that mission, we are committed to the highest standards in patient safety, quality and integrity. 

Within our Connected Health product group, we have set a new standard for digital health with our mymobility and ZBEdgeAnalytics platforms, which underpin a suite of digital healthcare products that transform Orthopaedic care for patients and clinicians alike. 

What You Can Expect

We're looking for an AI Engineer to join our Connected Health team at Zimmer Biomet. This is a fully remote, UK-based job. You'll design, build, deploy and improve generative AI and data-driven products that raise the quality of care and quality of life for orthopaedic patients worldwide.

You'll join our AI & Data Science team, which works across three areas:
• Product development: We develop prediction and decision-support algorithms, using classical ML and generative AI, for our patient- and clinician-facing applications.
• Product analysis: We help our product teams understand how people use our products, so they can make better decisions.
• Platform development: We build tooling and reusable infrastructure that supports AI and data-driven product development across Zimmer Biomet. We design it to follow best practice for Software as a Medical Device (SaMD).
We aim to keep improving, to communicate openly, and to enjoy ourselves along the way.

How You'll Create Impact

In this role you will work closely with machine learning scientists and application software engineers to bring advanced data insights to life. You'll build automation pipelines, deploy and serve both predictive models and generative AI systems, integrate third-party platforms and tooling, and design for observability and monitoring in production, whilst ensuring that we meet our regulatory commitments. 

Our work covers classical ML on structured, sensor and imaging data, and generative AI: retrieval-augmented generation and agentic systems. Because we build medical devices in a regulated context, quality, traceability and responsible AI matter at every step. You'll help us productionise these systems against standards including the EU AI Act and FDA guidance on AI/ML-enabled medical devices. 

You'll help shape our technical roadmap and influence how the Connected Health team moves forward with AI products. 

Today, our tooling revolves around: 
• Azure ML and Azure DevOps for model orchestration, CI/CD and development; 
• Python for data pipelines, machine learning pipelines and model serving; 
• MLflow (or similar) for experiment tracking and model registry, with monitoring for drift and performance in production; 
• LLM/GenAI tooling including foundation-model APIs, vector stores/retrieval, orchestration frameworks and evaluation harnesses; 
• Pulumi for infrastructure as code; 
• Occasionally C# to support integration between our internal systems. 

We also use modern developer tooling. Responsible use of AI coding assistants like Claude Code is part of how we work day-to-day. 

What Makes You Stand Out

• A passion for building generative AI and data-driven products to improve healthcare;
• The idea of shaping AI products excites you, and you’re comfortable working where requirements are still evolving; 
• Your background covers the majority of the end-to-end lifecycle of a AI/ML product, from containerisation, CI/CD, infrastructure deployment to debugging and monitoring models in production; 
• Hands-on experience with either classical ML or generative AI in production, and have a genuine interest in the other; 
• The ability to build cloud-native applications and are comfortable with infrastructure as code; 
• You can communicate analyses and technical ideas, and their value, to a range of audiences; 
• A drive to learn about new technologies and methodologies; 

If you don't meet every requirement but are excited by this role, we'd still like to hear from you!

Your Background

• A demonstrable background within healthcare data and/or delivering AI/ML in regulated spaces (SaMD, EU AI Act, FDA);
• Prior knowledge of evaluating and guard-railing generative AI systems 
• Experience with model monitoring, drift detection and responsible-AI practices (fairness, robustness, explainability).
• Industry experience as a Machine Learning, AI or Data Engineer;
• Comfortable programming with Python and packages associated with the AI/ML workflow; 

Travel & Logistic Expectations

This is a fully remote, UK-based role, and we actively support flexible working. We actively encourage team members to meet up and collaborate in person. Some of our colleagues are based in the U.S., so there will occasionally be a need to be available for evening meetings. 

To support our team members, we focus on development opportunities, Employee Resource Groups, a flexible working environment, location-specific competitive rewards, wellness incentives and a culture of recognition. We are committed to creating an environment where every team member feels included, respected, empowered and recognised. 

