We are seeking an experienced Electronic Security Small Works to install, commission and maintain Intruder, Access Control and CCTV systems in our Norfolk, Suffolk and Essex. In this Field based role, you will manage small projects independently, ensure compliance with PD6662/17 and NSI guidelines, and deliver high‑quality electronic security solutions through fault finding, remedial work and system upgrades.

This role is 37.5 hours Monday – Friday.

Salary: Up to £41033.80 , + commission

Benefits

• 25 days holiday plus bank holidays

• No on‑call requirement (optional participation available)

• Company van with private use option

• Extensive training and development opportunities

• Online GP for you and your family

• Pension scheme (5% employer contribution)

• Life assurance (4x salary)

• Employee referral scheme (£1,000)

• Discounts platform, wellbeing resources and recognition awards

Key Responsibilities

• Install, commission and maintain Intruder, access control and CCTV systems

• Produce quotations for small works and manage jobs from enquiry to completion

• Work with recommendations, commercial teams and Key Account Managers to progress opportunities

• Provide excellent customer service and clear communication throughout each project

• Identify upgrade and improvement opportunities for clients

• Manage you own diary and area.

What You Will Bring

• Proven experience as an electronic security Engineer with strong system knowledge

• Ability to work at height; IPAF 3a/3b advantageous

• Strong customer‑focused approach and ability to work independently

• Real team work ethic and a can-do attitude.

• Current Driving Licence

• Desire to work hard and be rewarded.

• Ideally located around Cambridgeshire to cover Cambs, Beds, Bucks, Herts, Norfolk & Suffolk

