We are recruiting a Recruitment Adviser on an 18-month fixed-term contract to focus on recruiting into our business services teams across the firm.

## About Macfarlanes

Macfarlanes is a pre-eminent law firm that serves a global client base in private capital, private wealth, M&A and disputes. Personal connection, an entrepreneurial spirit and a commitment to excellence are at the heart of our firm. These values drive our ability to deliver exceptional outcomes for our clients.

We are big enough to undertake the most complex and demanding mandates yet small enough to know each other well and to be agile, adapting to the needs of our clients. We seek to strengthen the firm by recruiting talented people from all backgrounds who want to build long-lasting and impactful careers with us. Our culture is challenging and supportive, creating an environment where individuals can thrive.

## What this means for you

Joining Macfarlanes means being part of a collaborative, approachable team who want you to succeed. You’ll be encouraged to get involved and be recognised for your contribution.

We take your development seriously. Our learning and development programmes are second to none and are designed to help you strengthen your skills.

Above all, you’ll be part of a firm where we all work together as part of a cohesive and supportive team, value your efforts and help you to thrive.

## The team

Attracting exceptional talent is fundamental to the firm’s success, and the Recruitment team is central to achieving this. Sitting within the wider Human Resources department, the team comprises a Senior Recruitment Manager, a Senior Recruitment Adviser, two Recruitment Advisers and a Recruitment Assistant. 

The team is responsible for recruiting all new hires across the fee-earning and business services groups on a permanent, contract and temporary basis, with the exception of trainee associates. This is an exciting opportunity for a commercially minded, curious and solutions-focussed individual to join a busy and friendly team. 

## The role

Key responsibilities include:

- building strong relationships with hiring managers and senior stakeholders across the firm's business services functions (Document Production, Finance, Human Resources, Innovation and AI, Marketing and Risk Management);
- developing an understanding of the firm and what we look for in a hire;
- working with each team to understand their function, objectives and culture;
- acting as a trusted adviser on recruitment matters, giving informed guidance on the external market, salary expectations and realistic timescales;
- helping hiring managers define the skills, experience and behaviours a role requires;
- drafting clear, accurate and appealing job descriptions, including for newly created roles where the scope still needs to be shaped, ensuring they are consistent with the firm’s framework and style;
- managing the full recruitment cycle, from taking the brief to offer acceptance;
- building relationships with key recruitment agencies, instructing on vacancies and encouraging a diverse shortlist of candidates;
- running screening calls and attending interviews, using structured, competency-based methods to assess candidates fairly and consistently, ensuring the firm makes the right hires;
- creating suitable interview exercises where appropriate;
- providing hiring managers and candidates with timely, constructive updates and feedback, managing expectations and ensuring a positive experience throughout;
- managing the offer process including advising on salaries and seeking internal approval; 
- proactively responding to business needs with speed and accuracy, seeking ideas and solutions;
- supporting recruitment team members during busy periods;
- contributing ideas to improve the recruitment process and the candidate experience; and
- maintaining up-to-date knowledge of current and relevant employment legislation.

This job description encompasses the main duties of the role and is by no means exhaustive. It is anticipated that duties may vary from time to time according to the needs of the department.

## The candidate

We are seeking an experienced recruitment professional with at least three years' experience, gained either as a consultant within a recruitment agency or as an in-house recruitment adviser, ideally recruiting for business services roles. They will have proven experience of end-to-end recruitment, managing multiple vacancies at once across a range of seniority levels, and of managing the offer process, including advising on salary and negotiating with candidates. 

The ideal candidate will also:

- give credible advice that instils confidence in stakeholders;
- be an excellent communicator, with experience of building strong relationships with stakeholders at all levels;
- be an effective prioritiser, comfortably and efficiently handling several tasks at once;
- thrive in a fast-paced environment;
- remain resilient and calm under pressure; and
- work with a high degree of accuracy.

