 WORK with us.
Senior Software Engineer

We at SCALED are passionate about solving real world problems, using cutting edge technologies and a human-centered design approach. We are a small, dynamic team of international talents, working semi-hybrid in central London.
We are currently recruiting a Senior Software Engineer to help us further develop our in-house ‘SCALED Software’. Our SCALED software automatically design ‘scale-like’ material solutions for flexible body protection using the power of parametric and computational design. 
If you are passionate about digital to physical product development and the sports sector, this is for you!

Role responsibilities
• Software Engineering for ‘SCALED Algorithm’ using Rhino, Grasshopper, C+, C#, Java

• Develop and maintain software tools that enable parametric design workflows

• Design, implement and test software applications and libraries

• Enhance and support Product Development through computational design

• Backend & Frontend Development of SCALED Software

• You will work closely with other engineers and designers to understand their needs and create solutions that meet their requirements.

• Write clean, maintainable and efficient code, develop GITHub inventory

• Developing a SCALED material library for efficient material solutions

• Create and maintain technical documentation.

• Participate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback.

• Keep up-to-date with the latest trends and technologies in the field of software engineering and parametric design.

• Participate in research and development for the company’s vision

Minimum requirements 
• Professional experience in Computational Design 

• Great understanding of Git and Github

• Great experience working with Visual studio 

• Proficiency in C#, C++ and JavaScript

• Knowledge of Rhinocommon 

• Working understanding of Mesh geometry (including Half Edge Data Structures) and computational design

Good to have
• Professional experience in 3D printing (FDM and SLS)

• High Experience in Grasshopper and Rhino

• Knowledge of C++/C# interoperability is an advantage

• Experience developing UI in C# or Javascript 

• Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex data into clear and compelling visualizations.

• Prior work experience in Game Design and development benefitial

At SCALED, we take immense pride in cultivating a work culture that fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Our employees are treated as valued members of the team, with ample opportunities for professional development and advancement. As for benefits, we offer a comprehensive package including competitive salary, health insurance, retirement plans, flexible work hours, and generous vacation time. At SCALED, we prioritize diversity and inclusion, firmly believing that a diverse workforce leads to better creativity and innovation. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone's voices are heard, respected, and celebrated. We actively promote equality, fairness, and the eradication of biases. Be a part of SCALED and experience a workplace where you can thrive professionally and personally, while being valued for your uniqueness.

