The Trade Desk is a global technology company and the world’s leading independent platform for digital advertising, with over 3,000 employees across more than 30 offices. Our technology helps advertisers reach the right audiences across the open internet — from streaming TV and podcasts to mobile apps, news, and more.&nbsp; 

Advertising powers the content people love. By making it more transparent, effective, and responsible, we help support trusted journalism, quality entertainment, and creators worldwide. The world’s brands and agencies rely on us to reach their customers and grow their businesses responsibly. 

The scale of our platform brings unique technical challenges — from processing massive datasets in real time to building systems that operate reliably on a global scale. When you work here, your impact is worldwide. We welcome diverse perspectives, encourage curiosity, and build teams that learn from one another. If you’re driven to solve meaningful challenges, we’d love to meet you.

The Director, Commercial&nbsp;Deals &amp; Pricing&nbsp;is the hands-on operational leader who partners directly with Sales and Business Development to structure, evaluate, and move individual deals through to approval. You&nbsp;are fluent&nbsp;in pricing,&nbsp;deal&nbsp;terms,&nbsp;commercial&nbsp;incentive structures,&nbsp;and&nbsp;margin math,&nbsp;and&nbsp;you're&nbsp;the person a seller calls when a deal needs to&nbsp;evolve from transactional discounting to a&nbsp;strategic&nbsp;value exchange partnership.&nbsp;&nbsp;

You'll&nbsp;work closely with Sales/BD, Finance, and commercial leadership to make sure deals are well-structured, properly documented, and move through approval efficiently,&nbsp;without compromising on margin or deal quality. The ideal candidate has strong deal finance instincts,&nbsp;experience&nbsp;working&nbsp;on enterprise-level accounts, and is equally comfortable partnering on complex, custom&nbsp;deals&nbsp;and driving teams to standardized models.&nbsp;

What&nbsp;you'll&nbsp;do&nbsp;

Deal-by-deal commercial support&nbsp;

• Serve as the primary&nbsp;strategic partner&nbsp;for Sales/BD on individual deal structuring, including&nbsp;pricing, packaging, discounting, credits, and non-standard terms.&nbsp;

• Review and stress-test deal economics (rate, spend commitments, margin impact)&nbsp;before deals move to approval.&nbsp;

• Advise sellers in real time on how to structure a deal&nbsp;using&nbsp;deal model&nbsp;templates&nbsp;and account&nbsp;data.&nbsp;

• Operate&nbsp;within existing commercial guardrails where possible,&nbsp;identify&nbsp;when a deal needs escalation or an exception, and drive alignment on a resolution.&nbsp;

Deal desk operations &amp; approvals&nbsp;

• Own day-to-day operation of the deal approval process: intake, triage, documentation review, and routing deals to the right approver based on the delegation of authority framework.&nbsp;

• Prepare individual deals for&nbsp;executive&nbsp;review,&nbsp;including&nbsp;your&nbsp;clear, data-driven&nbsp;recommendations.&nbsp;

• Track deals through the pipeline to resolution, following up with Sales, Finance, and approvers to keep things moving and unblock stalled deals.&nbsp;

• Maintain&nbsp;accurate, up-to-date records of deal terms, approvals, and exceptions in Salesforce and supporting tools.&nbsp;

Cross-functional coordination&nbsp;

• Work closely with Finance/Deal Finance to&nbsp;validate&nbsp;margin&nbsp;and spend assumptions on individual deals.&nbsp;

• Partner with Legal as needed on non-standard terms within specific deals.&nbsp;

• Escalate deals that fall outside existing guardrails to commercial leadership with a clear recommendation and supporting analysis.&nbsp;

• Act as a feedback channel from the field back to commercial leadership,&nbsp;surfacing recurring deal patterns, friction points, or gaps in existing guidance.&nbsp;

Quality, consistency &amp; tooling&nbsp;

• Ensure&nbsp;every deal that reaches approval has complete, standardized documentation.&nbsp;

• Use and help refine existing deal templates, calculators, and reporting tools.&nbsp;Development&nbsp;new frameworks where needed.&nbsp;

• Identify&nbsp;recurring issues or bottlenecks in the deal review process and suggest practical fixes.&nbsp;

What you bring to the table&nbsp;

• 8+ years of experience in deal desk, commercial operations, deal finance, or&nbsp;a related&nbsp;function, ideally in SaaS or ad tech.&nbsp;

• Strong, hands-on experience structuring and reviewing individual commercial deals, including&nbsp;pricing, discounting, incentive structures, and non-standard terms.&nbsp;

• Comfort working at deal volume, managing multiple live deals at once with strong attention to detail and turnaround time.&nbsp;

• Solid financial acumen. You understand&nbsp;margin math, spend commitments, and rate structures, and&nbsp;can&nbsp;explain&nbsp;the details&nbsp;clearly to sellers and approvers.&nbsp;

• Experience working directly with Sales/BD in a deal-support capacity; able to push back constructively on deal terms while&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;a good working relationship.&nbsp;

• Working knowledge of Salesforce and standard deal/commercial tooling.&nbsp;

• Clear, direct communication skills. You are&nbsp;comfortable summarizing deal recommendations for approvers, including senior leadership.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

